WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.383
There once was a woodcutter who lived in Germany.

2
00:00:04.384 --> 00:00:08.347
He had two children named Hansel and Gretel.

3
00:00:08.348 --> 00:00:11.832
They lived together in a house in the forest.

4
00:00:11.833 --> 00:00:17.288
During the winter the woodcutter would go deep into the forest to cut firewood.

5
00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:26.678
When he came home, he and Hansel and Gretel would take the firewood to town to sell it and buy food.

6
00:00:26.679 --> 00:00:35.655
"Good-bye, children," said the woodcutter. "I am going to cut firewood. I will come home tonight for dinner."

7
00:00:35.656 --> 00:00:45.672
"Good-bye, Father," said Hansel and Gretel. And they waved as their father walked away.

8
00:00:45.673 --> 00:00:49.263
Dinnertime came and the woodcutter did not come home.

9
00:00:49.264 --> 00:00:52.882
"Where is Father?" asked Gretel.

10
00:00:52.883 --> 00:00:59.766
"I don't know," said Hansel, "but we won't eat dinner until he comes home."

11
00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:08.572
They waited and waited and waited. They waited so long they fell asleep.

12
00:01:08.573 --> 00:01:12.361
When they woke up, the sun was shining through the windows.

13
00:01:12.362 --> 00:01:19.506
"Oh no!" said Hansel. "Father did not come home! Something must have happened.

14
00:01:19.507 --> 00:01:26.086
We must go look for him." They packed some bread to eat and walked into the woods.

15
00:01:26.087 --> 00:01:31.992
"Wait, Hansel. How will we find our way home?" asked Gretel.

16
00:01:31.993 --> 00:01:39.564
"Uhh . . . Oh! I will leave bread crumbs in the path to show us how to get home," said Hansel.

17
00:01:39.565 --> 00:01:42.329
"Good idea," Gretel said.

18
00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:47.084
They walked for hours and hours and hours.

19
00:01:47.085 --> 00:01:55.958
Because they had used their bread to show the way home, they had nothing to eat. "I am getting hungry," said Hansel.

20
00:01:55.959 --> 00:02:02.601
"Yes, and I am getting cold too," said Gretel. "It is getting late.

21
00:02:02.602 --> 00:02:08.108
Maybe we should go home. Maybe Father is waiting there for us."

22
00:02:08.109 --> 00:02:13.984
"Yes, maybe he is. Let's go home," Hansel agreed.

23
00:02:13.985 --> 00:02:19.847
But, when they turned around to go home, they did not know which way to go.

24
00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:25.009
"Oh no!" said Gretel. "Our bread crumbs are gone!

25
00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:27.618
How will we find our way home?"

26
00:02:27.619 --> 00:02:33.124
"The birds must have eaten all our crumbs," said Hansel.

27
00:02:33.125 --> 00:02:41.280
"Maybe home is this way," said Gretel. They walked and walked and walked.

28
00:02:41.281 --> 00:02:44.246
Finally they saw smoke coming from a chimney.

29
00:02:44.247 --> 00:02:49.672
"It must be Father!" the children cried, and they ran to the house.

30
00:02:49.673 --> 00:02:54.414
But the smoke was not their father's. It was a magical house.

31
00:02:54.415 --> 00:03:01.029
Its walls were made of cookies, its roof was made of peppermint, and the doors were made of chocolate.

32
00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:09.946
"Wow!" said Hansel and Gretel. And they began to eat the house.

33
00:03:09.947 --> 00:03:15.538
What Hansel and Gretel didn't know was that inside the house lived a witch.

34
00:03:15.539 --> 00:03:20.792
While Hansel was busy eating, the witch opened the door and grabbed him.

35
00:03:20.793 --> 00:03:27.297
"Who is eating my house?" asked the witch. She was very angry.

36
00:03:27.298 --> 00:03:31.896
"I didn't know it was your house," said Hansel.

37
00:03:31.897 --> 00:03:38.001
"We're very sorry," said Gretel. "Please let him go."

38
00:03:38.002 --> 00:03:43.596
"No. He has eaten my house, and now I will eat him."

39
00:03:43.597 --> 00:03:47.554
The witch dragged Hansel into a cage and locked him inside.

40
00:03:47.555 --> 00:03:52.251
"And you will be my servant," she said to Gretel.

41
00:03:52.252 --> 00:03:56.274
Then the witch laughed a terrible laugh.

42
00:03:56.275 --> 00:04:03.391
The witch fed Hansel lots and lots of food to make him fat, so that he would be a delicious dinner.

43
00:04:03.392 --> 00:04:11.410
But the witch had very old eyes that made everything seem blurry, and she could not see if Hansel was fat.

44
00:04:11.411 --> 00:04:21.301
So every day she would say to Hansel, "Put out your finger," and she would feel it to see if he was fat enough.

45
00:04:21.302 --> 00:04:25.882
Hansel was smart. He did not put out his finger when the witch asked.

46
00:04:25.883 --> 00:04:29.752
He saved a bone from his dinner and put that out instead.

47
00:04:29.753 --> 00:04:38.360
The witch would feel the bone and say, "Not fat enough. Maybe I will eat him tomorrow."

48
00:04:38.361 --> 00:04:47.098
Gretel cried every day. She didn't want her brother to be eaten. Finally the day came.

49
00:04:47.099 --> 00:04:52.532
"Put out your finger," the witch asked. Hansel put out the bone.

50
00:04:52.533 --> 00:04:57.446
"Still not fat enough. Well, I am not going to wait.

51
00:04:57.447 --> 00:05:03.246
I will eat you tonight!" When Gretel heard this, she cried even harder.

52
00:05:03.247 --> 00:05:07.454
"Stop crying, silly girl!" the witch said.

53
00:05:07.455 --> 00:05:13.847
"Crawl inside that oven and make a fire to cook dinner."

54
00:05:13.848 --> 00:05:22.341
Gretel was smart too. She knew the witch was trying to trick her, so she said, "I don't know how to climb into an oven."

55
00:05:22.342 --> 00:05:29.034
"Stupid girl," the witch said. "I will show you, and then you will do it."

56
00:05:29.035 --> 00:05:31.875
The witch climbed inside the oven to show Gretel.

57
00:05:31.876 --> 00:05:38.837
But just as she was inside, Gretel shut the oven door and locked it.

58
00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:46.167
"Let me out!" cried the witch. "I promise not to eat you! I'm very sorry.

59
00:05:46.168 --> 00:05:51.157
Please let me out!" But the children did not listen to her.

60
00:05:51.158 --> 00:05:59.915
Gretel freed Hansel from his cage and they ran away from the witch's candy house as fast as they could.

61
00:05:59.916 --> 00:06:06.463
They ran and ran and ran. They saw another chimney with smoke coming out.

62
00:06:06.464 --> 00:06:09.981
"We must be careful, Hansel," said Gretel.

63
00:06:09.982 --> 00:06:15.267
She did not want to meet another witch. They walked quietly up to the house.

64
00:06:15.268 --> 00:06:19.393
Just then the door opened and the woodcutter walked out.

65
00:06:19.394 --> 00:06:29.016
"Father! Father! Father!" they cried. And they ran to him with their arms open. He gave them a big hug.

66
00:06:29.017 --> 00:06:34.434
"Hansel! Gretel! Where have you been! I was so worried about you!"

67
00:06:34.435 --> 00:06:40.484
"We went looking for you, Father," said Gretel.

68
00:06:40.485 --> 00:06:46.676
"Yes, you didn't come home so we went to find you," said Hansel.

69
00:06:46.677 --> 00:06:54.164
"Ah, I'm sorry, children. I broke my leg and came home the next day.

70
00:06:54.165 --> 00:06:58.826
But you were gone. You must never go into the forest alone.

71
00:06:58.827 --> 00:07:02.726
There are dangerous things in the forest."

72
00:07:02.727 --> 00:07:08.473
"Yes, Father. There are dangerous things in the forest," they said.

73
00:07:08.474 --> 00:07:11.875
Hansel and Gretel went inside the house with their father.

74
00:07:11.876 --> 00:07:24.986
They decided to tell him about the witch. But first they would eat dinner.

